hadiths[6]{hadithnumber,text}:
"952","The hadith of Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi: that 'Uwaymir al-'Ajlani came to 'Asim ibn 'Adi al-Ansari and said to him: ""O 'Asim, what do you think about a man who finds another man with his wife—does he kill him and then you kill him, or how should he act? Ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about this for me."" So 'Asim asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked the questions and censured them, until what he heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ became burdensome for 'Asim. When 'Asim returned to his family, 'Uwaymir came to him and said: ""O 'Asim, what did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say to you?"" 'Asim said: ""You did not bring me any good; the Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked the question I asked him about."" 'Uwaymir said: ""By Allah, I will not desist until I ask him about it myself."" So 'Uwaymir went until he came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the midst of the people and said: ""O Messenger of Allah, what do you think about a man who finds another man with his wife—does he kill him and then you kill him, or how should he act?"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Allah has revealed concerning you and your wife, so go and bring her."" Sahl said: ""They invoked curses (li'an), and I was with the people at the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When they had finished, 'Uwaymir said: 'I would have lied against her, O Messenger of Allah, if I kept her.' So he divorced her three times before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded him to."""""
"953","""I want my money back, O Allah's Messenger (ﷺ)."" The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""You have no right to it. If you have spoken the truth, it (i.e., the Mahr) is a reward for what you have made lawful from her (sexual relations with her); and if you have told a lie against her, then that (money) is even less rightful for you to get back."""
"954","Narrated Ibn `Umar:\n\nThe Prophet (ﷺ) made a man and his wife carry out Lian, and the husband repudiated her child. So the \nProphet got them separated (by divorce) and decided that the child belonged to the mother only."
"955","Ibn `Abbas; said, Once Lian was mentioned before the Prophet (ﷺ) whereupon `Asim bin Adi said something and went away. Then a man from his tribe came to him"
"956","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, None has more sense of ghaira than Allah"
"957","A man came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said, My brother has some Abdominal trouble."" The Prophet (ﷺ) said to him ""Let him drink honey."" The man came for the second time and the Prophet (ﷺ) said to him"
